// 1) UceApplication
// Add inside model UceApplication:
//   requestId String @unique @map("request_id")
//
// Semantics:
// - requestId identifies one Apply command.
// - replay of the same requestId resolves the already-created Application rather than creating another row.
// - an intentional second Application uses a new requestId.

// 2) UceOutreachAttempt
// Add inside model UceOutreachAttempt:
//   requestId String @unique @map("request_id")
//
// Semantics:
// - requestId identifies one Brand Outreach execution command.
// - Email click #1 and Email click #2 are legitimate separate attempts and therefore use different requestIds.
// - replay/double-submit of one Email click uses the same requestId and must not create another Attempt.
// - Priority DM Brand confirmation creates at most one accepted Attempt for its requestId.
// - Priority DM scheduler/provider execution is protected by persisted Attempt identity/state, not by another frontend requestId.

// 3) UceCampaignShare
// Add inside model UceCampaignShare:
//   requestId String @unique @map("request_id")
//
// Semantics:
// - every deliberate Share action gets a new requestId and remains independent.
// - replay of the same Share command must not create duplicate Share evidence/tracking identity.

